# task-16 — ISO: make the installer medium boot (fix F-A / OF-1)

Plan: /home/mei/nixos/.omo/plans/thinkpad-zero-touch-install.md (todo 16)
Brief: /home/mei/nixos/.omo/ulw-execute/briefs/wave4-t16.md
Worktree: /home/mei/nixos-wt/thinkpad-zero-touch-install-wave4 (branch thinkpad-zero-touch-install/wave4)
Base: main 5d4052f  ->  Commit: 7689b0c  fix(iso): let the installer medium boot without the password validator
Tier: LIGHT (single-spot ISO-only module following the existing extendModules pattern; no open design decisions)

## Defect (F-A)
`initrd-nixos-activation` runs ALL `system.activationScripts` before switch-root. The live ISO's
`/` is a tmpfs, so `modules/nixos/bootstrap-password.nix`'s `bootstrapPasswordHash` validator
hard-fails (`missing /var/lib/nixos-bootstrap/mei-password.hash`), activation aborts before
writing `/etc`, and switch-root refuses (`os-release file is missing`) -> emergency mode.
`consumeBootstrapPassword` fails the same way.

## Change (2 files, ISO-only)
- modules/flake/iso-images.nix — added installer-only module `bootstrapPasswordInert` to the
  `extendModules` list:
  `system.activationScripts.bootstrapPasswordHash = lib.mkForce { deps = []; text = ""; };`
  `system.activationScripts.consumeBootstrapPassword = lib.mkForce { deps = []; text = ""; };`
  `modules/nixos/bootstrap-password.nix` was NOT touched. No third neutralization was needed:
  nixpkgs `update-users-groups.pl:241-247` only *warns* when `hashedPasswordFile` is absent under
  `mutableUsers=true` (observed at boot: `warning: password file '…mei-password.hash' does not exist`).
- tests/iso-autostart-vm.nix — removed the test-only `seed-bootstrap-password` initrd fixture
  (and its throwaway hash) so the VM boots the config AS SHIPPED; kept the memory/cores overrides
  and every assertion.

